                "submission_id": "submission:correctness-review:1:2e52b155",
                "summary": "VERIFIED defect: public/icons/licences.json:43 records sprechen.svg as 'Drawn ... (commit 5fd5bfd, 2026-11-22)', but git ls-tree 5fd5bfd public/icons has no sprechen.svg; it was added in 85dcded (NG-30). The machine-checked provenance record the task exists to create is wrong for one file; fix: cite commit 85dcded for sprechen.svg. Second: docs/assets.md:33-34 says any licence that allows redistribution in a public MIT repository may be added without an owner decision, while test/assets.test.mjs:24-25 rejects every non-MIT licence; align the doc sentence with the test (only MIT without an owner decision) or relax the test. Non-blocking: docs/assets.md:50-52 states in present tense that the caregiver area warns and the board falls back, though the import (NG-8673323346005092805) is unbuilt; the test does not check licenceFile. Otherwise acceptance criteria met: assets.md states the 2026-11-23 owner decision, METACOM/ARASAAC reasons and on-device import rules; test/assets.test.mjs:12-15 deepEquals sorted readdir (minus licences.json) to the listed files, so it fails for missing, extra and duplicate entries; README links docs/assets.md and names MIT. Shipping dist/icons/licences.json is harmless: public/sw.js precache list is hand-written and excludes it, scripts/offline-smoke.mjs fetches only sw.js plus that list, and test/bootstrap.test.mjs:217 excludes it from the icons-must-be-precached check.",
